@prefix trn:  <http://purl.org/stuff/transmissions/> .
@prefix dsp:  <http://purl.org/stuff/transmissions/plugins/downspout/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix pu:   <http://purl.org/stuff/plugin-universe/> .

dsp:voxmod a trn:PluginProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Voxmod" ;
    rdfs:comment "Vocoder, ring modulator and live convolution cross-synthesis. Inputs 1/2 are the modulator/source, inputs 3/4 the analysed carrier and live IR feed. Mix balances ring against vocoder; Conv Mix fades that pair against sliding-window FFT frame multiplication with source and IR feedback. Ring, vocoder and convolution each have a Level control at unity by default; the convolution branch is peak-limited to keep feedback stable. Five CCs drive the legacy engines." ;
    trn:bundleName "voxmod.vst3" ;
    trn:vendor "danja" ;
    trn:role trn:AudioEffect ;
    trn:accepts trn:Audio, trn:ControlMidi ;
    trn:produces trn:Audio ;
    trn:caution "The port roles are load-bearing: inputs 1/2 are the source the vocoder colours and inputs 3/4 are the carrier it analyses and the convolver's live IR. The convolver needs a signal on both pairs; silence on 3/4 gives no wet output. Live 1/2 In and 3/4 In meters show whether the host routed both buses. Set Carrier to internal osc, or Sync, to drive the vocoder from inputs 1/2 alone." ;
    trn:recommendedAfter dsp:drift ;
    pu:supportedPlatform pu:Windows, pu:MacOS, pu:Linux .
